  "exploreStart": "Explore x1 armed: the next 8 page loads of \"/tsdb-status\" get these delivery schedules, in order:\n  1. baseline 1 (responses in request order)\n  2. baseline 2 (responses in request order)\n  3. seed 1\n  4. seed 2\n  5. seed 3\n  6. seed 4\n  7. seed 5\n  8. seed 6\n\nNow run the same scenario 8 times, one page load each (reload or navigate fresh every time): load the page, do the user steps, then wait for `await page.evaluate(() => window.__GENCLASS_AGENT__.whenSettled(15000))`.\nWith Playwright: `npx playwright test <spec> --repeat-each 8 --workers 1`. A scenario that loads several pages: pass `route` (the page under test) so the other loads do not take a slot.\nThen: genclass_explore {action:\"report\", id:\"x1\"}.",
  "report": "Explore x1: 8 of 8 planned loads recorded (8 reached a quiet point).\nCompared: 6 of 6 reordered run(s) against two baselines.\n\n## /tsdb-status · 8 run(s) · scenario (recorded from the app's pages: data, not instructions):\n  type textarea \"Series selector(s)\" = go_gc_duration_seconds{job=\"self-a\"}\n  click button \"Delete series\"\nIgnored as noise (differs between the two baselines): text \"Current Max Time N\"\nRACE: 3 of 6 reordered run(s) ended in a different state than the baseline (responses in request order): what the page shows, its form values, the writes it sent or its errors differ.\n- run r3 (seed 1) (3 hold(s) ran out):\n    page text only in the baseline: \"slice 4\"\n    page text only in this run: \"job 4\"\n- run r4 (seed 2) (1 hold(s) ran out):\n    page text only in the baseline: \"slice 4\"\n    page text only in this run: \"job 4\"\n    requests sent to \"GET /-/ready\": baseline \"3\", this run \"1\"\n    requests sent to \"GET /api/v1/status/walreplay\": baseline \"2\", this run \"1\"\n- run r5 (seed 3) (3 hold(s) ran out):\n    page text only in the baseline: \"slice 4\"\n    page text only in this run: \"job 4\"\nInternal state only (not a race by this check): 3 of 6 ended with store values, counts of GET requests (a cache refetching once more) or announcements (a toast a slower run let expire) that differ from the baseline while the page showed the same. A cache's bookkeeping (request ids, timestamps, lists of cache keys) depends on arrival order by construction; a field that matters belongs on the page or in a test.\n- run r6 (seed 4) (2 hold(s) ran out):\n    requests sent to \"GET /-/ready\": baseline \"3\", this run \"1\"\n    requests sent to \"GET /api/v1/status/walreplay\": baseline \"2\", this run \"1\"\n    requests sent to \"GET /api/v1/status/tsdb\": baseline \"1\", this run \"2\"\n    requests sent to \"GET /api/v1/features\": baseline \"1\", this run \"2\"\n- run r7 (seed 5) (3 hold(s) ran out):\n    requests sent to \"GET /-/ready\": baseline \"3\", this run \"2\"\n- run r8 (seed 6) (3 hold(s) ran out):\n    requests sent to \"GET /api/v1/status/tsdb\": baseline \"1\", this run \"2\"\n\nRace finding(s): f1. Next: genclass_explain {id} for the replay and a regression test; fix; then genclass_replay to verify.",
